# Project Architecture

Stack: npm workspaces · Vite/React/Chakra · Express/Prisma/SQLite · TanStack Query + Router · Zustand

## Layout

```
client/   UI only
server/   API only
dev-manager/  optional Electron panel
.env      single root env file
```

## Server layers (strict)

- `routes/` — HTTP + Zod parse. No Prisma.
- `schemas/` — Zod only.
- `repositories/` — Prisma only. No Express types.
- `services/` — business logic + external APIs.
- `errors/AppError` — typed HTTP errors.
- `middleware/errorHandler` — last middleware.

## Client layers (strict)

- `api/client.ts` — generic fetch.
- `api/*.ts` — endpoint wrappers.
- `hooks/` — React Query. Server state lives here.
- `store/` — Zustand for UI state only.
- `components/ui/` — form primitives.
- `pages/` — route screens.
- `theme/` + `styles.css` — design tokens.

## Do

- Prefer small focused files.
- Match existing naming and import style.
- Use Turkish UI copy if the product is Turkish.
- Keep CORS allowing localhost + optional `.ts.net`.

## Don't

- Don't put Prisma in routes.
- Don't put React Query calls deep inside presentational components without hooks.
- Don't invent a second env file under `server/` (root `.env` only).
- Don't use `window.confirm` — use delete confirm bubble pattern.
- Don't default to Tailwind; this stack uses Chakra UI v2.
